(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[10 1 "// memoryview: a port of CPython 3.14.10's Objects/memoryobject.c (queue 473, the main session's 456-1 (a); PY5e's"] [11 1 "// minimum, PY6a's casts and queues 249-304's fixes before it). A view is a Py_buffer (Buffer): its exporter's memory"] [12 1 "// (BufMem: a Go exporter's bytes, or the C world's address space for a C exporter's view, kept in place), the address"] [13 1 "// of its first item, its length in bytes, item size, format, shape, strides and suboffsets (PIL-style indirect"] [14 1 "// arrays), and the flags init_flags computes from them. Indexing, slicing (init_slice), tolist, tobytes in C, Fortran or"] [15 1 "// any order (PyBuffer_ToContiguous), cast (cast_to_1D, cast_to_ND), the comparisons (memory_richcompare: unpack_cmp's"] [16 1 "// native formats, the struct module's for any other), hash, count, index and memory_getbuf are memoryobject.c's"] [17 1 "// algorithms over that description. Ported from CPython 3.14.10; the PSF's license, LICENSE.md."] [21 1 "// BufMem is a view's address space: a Go exporter's bytes (addresses its offsets) or the C world's memory (arbace/pyctypes)."] [23 2 "// Read is n bytes at addr; never fails (bytes past a Go exporter that shrank read as zeros)"] [25 2 "// Write is the n bytes at addr for writing in place"] [27 2 "// Ptr is the pointer stored at addr (ADJUST_PTR's *((char**)ptr))"] [31 1 "// goMem is a Go exporter's memory: its bytes (asBytes, read at each access), written through writableBuffer."] [61 1 "// Buffer is a Py_buffer (Include/pybuffer.h): Format \"\" is NULL (\"B\"), Suboffsets nil is NULL; Shape and Strides are"] [62 1 "// complete in a view's (mbuf_add_view's init_shape_strides), possibly nil in a master an exporter filled."] [73 1 "// The memoryview's flags (Include/memoryobject.h) and the getbuffer requests (Include/pybuffer.h)."] [94 1 "// mvFlagsFullRO is PyBUF_FULL_RO, the flags memoryview() and bytes() ask a __buffer__ for."] [97 1 "// MemoryView is a PyMemoryViewObject: its view, its flags, the managed buffer it is registered with."] [101 2 "// exporter is what obj shows when it is not view.Obj (PEP 688: the object whose __buffer__ made the view;"] [102 2 "// _interpreters' XIBufferView)"] [105 2 "// mbuf is the export the view holds with the views made from it (queue 249, buffer_export.go): nil when its"] [106 2 "// exporter counts none"] [108 2 "// exports is the view's own (memory_getbuf's, and memory_hash's over the exporter's hash): release() refused while"] [109 2 "// any; hash once computed (queue 249)"] [113 2 "// bufOf is the view whose __buffer__ made this one (queue 304: __release_buffer__'s check, wrap_releasebuffer)"] [115 2 "// restricted is _Py_MEMORYVIEW_RESTRICTED (queue 475): the view releasebuffer_call_python hands a class's"] [116 2 "// __release_buffer__, from which no new view may be made (CHECK_RESTRICTED)"] [120 1 "// BufferShaper is an exporter whose buffer is not a 1-D array of bytes (queue 260): Py_buffer's format, itemsize and"] [121 1 "// shape (ndim its length; strides NULL, so C-contiguous) as its getbufferproc gives them, ctypes' PyCData_NewGetBuffer."] [126 1 "// shaperOf is o's BufferShaper (or its built-in value's), nil when o's buffer is plain bytes."] [137 1 "// BufferFormatter is an exporter of a 1-D buffer whose items are not bytes (queue 304): its Py_buffer's format, a"] [138 1 "// native one (\"\" for 'B'), as array_buffer_getbuf gives an array's typecode."] [143 1 "// exporterFormat is the format of o's 1-D buffer (BufferFormatter's), \"B\" for bytes."] [157 1 "// restrictedErr is CHECK_RESTRICTED's error."] [162 1 "// releasedErr is CHECK_RELEASED's error."] [167 1 "// hasIndex is _PyIndex_Check: an int, or a type with __index__."] [175 1 "// ---- formats ----"] [177 1 "// mvItemSizes are get_native_fmtchar's formats and their native sizes (64-bit Linux)."] [181 1 "// mvFmtChar is a format without its optional '@'."] [189 1 "// mvFmtSize is get_native_fmtchar: a native format's item size, false when f is none (3.15.2: also \"Zf\" and \"Zd\","] [190 1 "// the complex formats; 3.14.10: one character only)."] [205 1 "// mvByteFmt is IS_BYTE_FORMAT of a native format."] [211 1 "// adjustFmt is adjust_fmt: the view's format without '@' when it is one character (3.15.2: or a complex code), else"] [212 1 "// NotImplementedError."] [221 1 "// u64 is PyLong_FromUnsignedLongLong."] [229 1 "// unpackNative is unpack_single of the item b (its format's size) of native format f."] [272 1 "// unpack is unpack_single of the item at addr (CHECK_RELEASED_AGAIN first)."] [284 1 "// pack is pack_single of v into the item at addr, the view checked again after the conversion (gh-92888, queue 304: a"] [285 1 "// value's __index__, __float__ or __bool__ that releases the view leaves its memory alone)."] [306 1 "// mvPack is pack_single (Objects/memoryobject.c) of v into b, one item of native format f (queue 286): the integer"] [307 1 "// formats by __index__ (type_error_int, value_error_int), the floats by PyFloat_AsDouble, '?' by truth, 'c' one byte;"] [308 1 "// fix_error_int's messages for the conversions' errors."] [351 31 "// 3.15.2's complexes: the struct module's F and D"] [410 12 "// PyLong_AsVoidPtr: a negative pointer as PyLong_AsLongLong's"] [416 11 "// B H I L Q N"] [426 1 "// ---- the view's structure ----"] [428 1 "// isContig is _IsCContiguous ('C') and _IsFortranContiguous ('F') of a buffer with strides (NULL strides: C)."] [464 1 "// IsContiguous is PyBuffer_IsContiguous."] [478 1 "// initStrides is init_strides_from_shape; initFortranStrides init_fortran_strides_from_shape."] [501 1 "// initLen is init_len."] [510 1 "// at is the address of the item at idx (PyBuffer_GetPointer: strides, then ADJUST_PTR per dimension)."] [522 1 "// each calls fn with the address of every item in order 'C' (the last index fastest) or 'F' (the first)."] [555 1 "// ToContiguous is PyBuffer_ToContiguous: the buffer's bytes in order 'C', 'F' or 'A' (the memory as it is when"] [556 1 "// contiguous in either order, else C's)."] [572 1 "// fromContiguous writes data, the items in C order, into b's items (copy_buffer's destination)."] [586 1 "// equivShape is equiv_shape; equivFormat equiv_format."] [606 1 "// copyBuffer is copy_buffer (and copy_single): src's items into dest's, atomically, both of one structure."] [614 1 "// clone is a copy of the view's description, its arrays its own."] [624 1 "// initFlags is init_flags."] [654 1 "// viewFrom is mbuf_add_view: a new view of src (init_shared_values, init_shape_strides, init_suboffsets, init_flags)"] [655 1 "// registered with mb."] [692 1 "// derive registers nv, a view made from m (a slice, a cast, memoryview(m), toreadonly), with m's managed buffer."] [699 1 "// copyView is mbuf_add_view(self->mbuf, &self->view)."] [705 1 "// itemsize is view->itemsize."] [708 1 "// ndim is view->ndim."] [711 1 "// View is the view's Py_buffer (not to be modified)."] [714 1 "// cBytes is the view's memory when it is C-contiguous (a \"w*\" or \"y*\" argument's bytes, in place), false when it is"] [715 1 "// not or the view is released."] [730 1 "// ---- construction ----"] [732 1 "// newGoView is the view of a Go exporter's buffer (bytes, bytearray, array, mmap, a ctypes object, ...): 1-D of its"] [733 1 "// format, or the shape a BufferShaper gives, C-contiguous, read-only when the exporter is not writable."] [741 36 "// queue 260: the exporter's format, itemsize and shape"] [763 3 "// slot_bf_releasebuffer (queue 475): a class over a built-in exporter whose __release_buffer__ is Python's"] [764 3 "// gets, when the export is released, a restricted view of the buffer, then the built-in's own release"] [773 1 "// NewBytesView is a memoryview of the bytes b (format 'B'), read-only."] [780 1 "// NewBufferView is a memoryview of a Py_buffer an exporter filled (PyMemoryView_FromBuffer, _PyManagedBuffer_FromObject"] [781 1 "// of a C type; arbace/pyctypes): its master's missing shape and strides reconstructed, release called once the last"] [782 1 "// view made from it is released (mbuf_release's PyBuffer_Release), exporter what obj shows when not info.Obj."] [796 1 "// bufferOf is a class's __buffer__(flags): its memoryview, nil when the type has none (PY7: memoryview() and bytes()"] [797 1 "// of such an object raised TypeError)."] [822 1 "// ExtBufferHook is the buffer of an object whose type a C extension made with bf_getbuffer (arbace/pyctypes, queue"] [823 1 "// 270b): its view for the request flags (found false when the type has none), as bufferOf's of a class's __buffer__."] [826 1 "// releaseBuffer is PyBuffer_Release of a view bufferOf got: the exporter's __release_buffer__(view), when it has one."] [835 1 "// releasebufferCallPython is typeobject.c's releasebuffer_call_python: self's __release_buffer__ called with mv, the"] [836 1 "// view its __buffer__ returned (a wrapper's), else (mv nil) a view of master made restricted (PyMemoryView_FromBuffer,"] [837 1 "// its obj NULL; _Py_MEMORYVIEW_RESTRICTED) and released after the call. Errors are unraisable, and the exception being"] [838 1 "// handled stays (PyErr_GetRaisedException ... PyErr_SetRaisedException)."] [862 1 "// MemoryViewFromObject is PyMemoryView_FromObjectAndFlags: a view of o's buffer (a memoryview's own, registered with"] [863 1 "// its managed buffer), else TypeError with prefix (\"memoryview: \" for memoryview()'s, \"\" for PyObject_GetBuffer's)."] [878 38 "// picklebuf_getbuf: the object's own buffer"] [884 28 "// a C type's bf_getbuffer: its own managed buffer"] [893 3 "// the export of a class's __buffer__ (slot_bf_getbuffer): memory_getbuf of the view it returned, obj the"] [894 3 "// object; its __release_buffer__ called when the last view goes"] [911 1 "// goViewFlags is a Go exporter's getbufferproc as memoryview sees it (bytes_buffer_getbuffer, bytearray_getbuffer,"] [912 1 "// ...: PyBuffer_FillInfo's checks), the view's managed buffer the export: what memoryview(o) gives for a built-in, and"] [913 1 "// a built-in's __buffer__ (wrap_buffer's _PyMemoryView_FromBufferProc, which calls the built-in's own getbufferproc,"] [914 1 "// never a subclass's __buffer__)."] [936 1 "// getBufferView is PyObject_GetBuffer(o, PyBUF_FULL_RO) for pyi's own users: a view to release once used."] [950 1 "// GetBuf is memory_getbuf: the view's Py_buffer for the request flags (an export of the view until ReleaseBuf)."] [997 1 "// ReleaseBuf is memory_releasebuf."] [1004 1 "// GetContiguous is PyMemoryView_GetContiguous: a view of obj's buffer when contiguous in order (buffertype PyBUF_READ"] [1005 1 "// 0x100 or PyBUF_WRITE 0x200), else a view of a contiguous copy (memory_from_contiguous_copy)."] [1040 1 "// ---- release ----"] [1042 1 "// release is memoryview.release(): the exporter's buffer released once."] [1064 1 "// unusable is the view's CHECK_RELEASED, and its exporter's own check when it has one (queue 204: an mmap closed under"] [1065 1 "// the view raises ValueError \"mmap closed or invalid\", where CPython's mmap refuses the close; pyi counts no exports)."] [1080 1 "// isReadonly is view->readonly."] [1083 1 "// exportedObj is the view's obj attribute: view->obj (None when it has none: PyMemoryView_FromBuffer's)."] [1094 1 "// data is the view's bytes in C order (PyBuffer_ToContiguous 'C': bytes(m), tobytes())."] [1102 1 "// BytesLike makes a memoryview a bytes-like object (asBytes): a copy of its bytes."] [1110 1 "// ---- indexing ----"] [1112 1 "// lookupDim is lookup_dimension."] [1129 1 "// ptrFromTuple is ptr_from_tuple."] [1148 1 "// item is memory_item."] [1170 1 "// itemMulti is memory_item_multi."] [1189 1 "// initSlice is init_slice of dimension dim."] [1214 1 "// isMultislice is is_multislice; isMultiindex is_multiindex."] [1241 1 "// subscript is memory_subscript."] [1289 1 "// assSub is memory_ass_sub."] [1325 49 "// one-dimensional: copy_single from the rvalue's buffer"] [1336 19 "// CHECK_RELEASED_INT_AGAIN"] [1358 1 "// ---- lists, bytes ----"] [1360 1 "// tolistRec is tolist_rec (tolist_base at the last dimension)."] [1382 1 "// tolist is memoryview_tolist_impl."] [1397 1 "// ---- comparison ----"] [1399 1 "// structUnpacker is struct_get_unpacker: the struct module's unpacking of one item of format f."] [1420 1 "// nativeChar is get_native_fmtchar's character of a format, \"\" when it is none."] [1428 1 "// unpackCmp is unpack_cmp of the items p and q, f their common native format (\"\" for the struct module's unpackers)."] [1466 1 "// richCompare is memory_richcompare."] [1516 2 "// the items in C order, side by side (cmp_rec: same shape)"] [1542 1 "// ---- the type ----"] [1553 2 "// memory_hash (queue 249): a read-only byte view's hash is its bytes' (hash(b'..')), the exporter hashed first with"] [1554 2 "// the view exported meanwhile (gh-142664: a re-entrant __hash__ that releases the view gets BufferError)"] [1592 33 "// memory_repr"] [1618 2 "// memoryview_tobytes_impl: order 'C' (None), 'F' or 'A'"] [1647 2 "// cast (queue 263): memoryview_cast_impl over cast_to_1D and cast_to_ND"] [1663 2 "// memoryview_hex_impl (queue 304): sep and bytes_per_sep as bytes.hex's (pystrhex.c), the view exported meanwhile"] [1664 2 "// (gh-143195: a sep whose __len__ releases the view gets BufferError)"] [1690 2 "// memoryview_count_impl: over the view's iteration (memory_iter's checks)"] [1700 10 "// memoryview_count_impl over memory_iter"] [1716 2 "// memoryview_index_impl"] [1780 55 "// memory_enter: CHECK_RELEASED"] [1786 2 "// _from_flags (memoryview__from_flags_impl): PyMemoryView_FromObjectAndFlags"] [1798 2 "// __buffer__ and __release_buffer__ (memory_getbuf, memory_releasebuf as slot wrappers; queue 304): a view of"] [1799 2 "// memory_getbuf's Py_buffer for flags (_PyMemoryView_FromBufferProc), obj the view; its release"] [1820 2 "// bytes' and bytearray's __buffer__ (bytes_buffer_getbuffer, bytearray_getbuffer as slot wrappers; queue 328:"] [1821 2 "// collections.abc.Buffer